tainly like possible  in my game what I've tried to do is gone  back and forth on this a lot but  ultimately again I want to focus on the  future as a way to step aside from these  partisan barriers and I think I'm going  to try to do it in a non-partisan way  although my hope is that those five  issue areas will generally  only really apply to organizations that  are trying to move in a more positive  direction for everyone and especially  given I think the state of the  Republican Party right now with so many  people feeling politically homeless and  that was something that I saw a lot and  my research last summer I don't want to  say it's a progressive thing because I  think it's something that people from  across the political spectrum might be  able to get behind so yeah the the goal  is to be non partisan generally  organizing around the idea of creating a  better community in the future Lisa  Oh  yeah that's a great question and  something I didn't touch on so like I  said I want to start with about 50  different sort of tutorials on different  things you can do that you know would  include yeah baby if you like to knit  this is something and then there will be  an onboarding process you'll be able to  say like I like doing these things and  then it'll give you some initial  suggestions but you can also add those  as you level up and not only can you add  tactics you can also add campaigns and  admissions and adding missions I think  could be a core piece of game back play  that ties into the team component  because the way it works is you you  create the mission and then you actually  get points for not only you doing it but  anybody else who does that mission so  it's trying to get people to come up  with more creative ways to engage and  part of what I think could be  interesting out of this is just creating  a big database of all of those  possibilities so yeah I definitely want  it to be something that can expand  all right thank you  [Applause]
 

